      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What it is"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "key": "b2",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "E621 Monosodium glutamate (MSG) is the sodium salt of glutamic acid, produced by fermentation. It is a flavour enhancer that adds a savoury, umami taste."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "key": "b3",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why it is in your food"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "key": "b4",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Manufacturers use it as flavour enhancer."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "key": "b5",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What we hold on it"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "key": "b6",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This page is about the record we hold on this additive: who has written about it, and where you can read them."
        }
      ]
